// Three illusory duplicates via the same BasicSummon + PhantomIllusion
// "shared-illusion decoy" recipe minor_illusion_image.ron/major_image.ron
// already ship (common/src/comp/phantom_illusion.rs) -- not new engine
// work, but the first Lane-A dispatch of BasicSummon per plan Q6, flagged
// for reviewer attention accordingly. phantom_illusion.rs's own module doc
// already documents "attacking is the only reveal trigger" (a phantasm
// dispels the instant it's struck, for everyone watching) -- an exact
// mechanical match for "each strike that lands on a decoy shatters it
// harmlessly". Scope narrowed: a decoy is a separate targetable entity
// summoned near the caster, not a redirect of an attack aimed at the
// caster's own body (no such redirect mechanism exists); decoys render as a
// generic phantasm placeholder body, not a likeness of the caster (same
// "visual half only" scoping major_image.ron's own comment documents --
// cloning a player's exact appearance onto a summoned NPC is new work).
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    cast_duration: 0.2,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 3,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 2.0),
        body: Object(Pebble),
        scale: None,
        has_health: false,
        use_npc_name: false,
        loadout_config: None,
        skillset_config: None,
        duration: Some((
            secs: 60,
            nanos: 0,
        )),
        alignment: Some(Passive),
        with_agent: false,
        incorporeal: true,
        phantom_illusion: true,
        delete_after_expiry: true,
    ),
)
